        "original_id": "f60081cd-ec10-5973-a5fd-9e42e3b69ec4",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Osireion, Abydos\n- People: Seti I, Ramesses I, Sitre, Ramesses II\n- Roles: Pharaoh\n- Organizations: New Kingdom Nineteenth Dynasty of Egypt\n\nFacts:\n- The Osireion is located at Abydos, to the rear of the temple of Seti I.\n- Menmaatre Seti I, also called Sethos I in Greek, was a pharaoh of the New Kingdom Nineteenth Dynasty of Egypt.\n- Seti I was the son of Ramesses I and Sitre.\n- Seti I was the father of Ramesses II.",
